# Renders the partial root paths this extension contributes to "page.10", the page object
# of the site package.
#
# The other setup fixture next to this one replaces "page.10" wholesale with
# "styles.content.get", so the block is inert there and nothing would see a key that is
# wrong or missing. This file is included instead of it, and without a page object of its
# own: "page.10" then carries configuration but no cObject, renders nothing, and the two
# copied values are what the test reads.
page = PAGE
page {
  5 = TEXT
  5.value < page.10.partialRootPaths.-1758484804
  5.wrap = <div id="shared-partial-path">|</div>

  6 = TEXT
  6.value < page.10.partialRootPaths.1693651551
  6.wrap = <div id="own-partial-path">|</div>
}
